Defination - Class is a structural representation which represents named group of properties and functions.

we can create multiple objects from a single class.

Q) why classes?
  It represents structural representation and provides code reusability and promotes code organisation.

Q) Can a class exists without Objects ?
    yes, bcoz a class is just a template which represents structure,
    it doesn't hold the actual object itself.

Q) How can we access Class Members without Object?
    we know that  members which are only related to class not objects are declared as static.
    we know that Static members are related to class not dependent on objets.
    There by, Static members are resolved at compile time rather than runtime.

    Ex:-
    Class Student{
        int age;
        String name;
        static String School_name="SGRCS";
    }
    public static void main(String args[]){
        System.out.println(Student.School_name); // here by static members are accessed by creating a single copy of var, shared by all instances of a class by class name without object creation.
    }
